    "done_when": "format_sign_report in imas_ambix/data/cocos_convention.py prints MAST's fixed blocks only for the MAST level-2 cohort: the coefficient classification, the determinable relative-sign products, the COCOS 3 versus 4 note, the recommendation and the Ip-like consequence. For any other cohort it states the classification its own rows support: sigma_Bp from the raw absolute-loop response, sigma_rho_theta_phi from the q relation, sigma_R_phi_Z undetermined. The flux exponent is no longer MAST's hard-coded 0 for a row whose equilibrium carries no psi. Such a row records e_Bp as undetermined, the declared-flux-exponent check is left unscored for it with that reason, and the JT-60SA verdict therefore lists every candidate the scored relations leave (1, 2, 11 and 12 if nothing else decides it). The report names E101011's G-EQDSK (section 7) as the source that would fix e_Bp. MAST_LEVEL2_SIGN_TABLE scores and MAST's report text are unchanged, pinned by a test. New tests pin the single-absolute-loop consensus (an agreeing one-loop row is not a violation) and the one-interval alignment tolerance (a gap of one sampling interval is accepted, a larger one refused). scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py regenerates docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-sign-cohort.html and its figure. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the bundle discovered from maps/jt-60sa and IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset, uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py exits 0 and the cohort script exits 0, each captured once to a log with the revision and command on its first lines, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
